select 'tdr', 'TDR (Transferable Development Rights)', 'Development potential separated from one plot and used on another, issued as a certificate.', 'When land is surrendered for a public purpose (such as a road or reservation), the owner can receive TDR instead of cash compensation. The TDR can be sold and loaded on an eligible receiving plot, subject to road-width-based limits.', 'An owner surrenders a strip for road widening and receives a Development Right Certificate, which a developer elsewhere buys to add floor area to their project.', 'UDCPR, Maharashtra',
